    "narrative": "The offensive core for the Zurich Zebras today is anchored by **Junior Caminero**, who projects as our premier start with a score of 83.69. Facing an exploitable arm in J. Lopez (5.06 xERA), **Caminero** benefits from a high-leverage 3rd-hole assignment and an elite xwOBA of 0.376, making him the centerpiece of our daily production expectations. **Yordan Alvarez** follows closely at 76.86; despite a slight park penalty, his elite 0.467 xwOBA and favorable wind conditions in his matchup against Tidwell position him as the most reliable source for high-ceiling power. **Caleb Durbin** also grades out as a strong play (62.57) against Taillon, as he continues to be a vital asset in maintaining our competitive edge in the scarcest category: stolen bases.\n\nThe middle of the order presents a tight cluster of decision-making, with **Kyle Schwarber**, **Carson Benge**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Lars Nootbaar** all hovering near the 57\u201360 score range. **Schwarber** warrants a start primarily due to his leadoff slotting against Dobbins, which offsets his park-adjusted baseline. **Benge** serves as the most volatile asset in the group; while his metrics remain strong against Elder, the 37% rain risk looms as a legitimate threat to his total plate appearances. With **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Colt Keith** all unavailable due to scheduled off-days or rest, our depth is thinner than usual, placing the burden of run production squarely on the shoulders of this active unit. Should we need to pivot for late-inning pinch-hitting or defensive switches, we retain **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** on the periphery, though none currently offer a profile that would have displaced our starters today. **Josh Smith** remains our lowest-scored active starter (51.05) due to his low lineup position, but he holds a spot solely for his high recency-based efficiency.",
